## Pages and sections

Every Markdown file in `content/docs` becomes a page. A folder creates a section in the sidebar.

```text
content/docs/
├── introduction.md
├── getting-started.md
└── guides/
    ├── _index.md
    └── workflow.md
```

Use `_index.md` to name and order a section. Its frontmatter follows the same shape as a regular page:

```md
---
title: "Guides"
description: "Complete workflows for common jobs"
order: 4
---
```

## Keep the hierarchy shallow

Two levels are enough for most product documentation. Add a nested group only when several pages share a clear purpose.
